{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0158weACtA7NqojYf7iXt1Yk","type":"tool_result","content":"    # Changes only when the athlete edits their profile, so it sits inside the cached prefix.\n    return \"\\n\".join([\n        f\"Athlete: {a.name} (id {a.user_id}), sport: {a.sport}\",\n        \"Zones: \" + \", \".join(f\"{k} {v}\" for k, v in a.zones.items()),\n        f\"Goal: {a.goal}\",\n        f\"Language: {a.lang}\",\n        \"Long-term facts:\",\n    ])\n\n\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    \"\"\"Static-first system prompt, so a memory write never invalidates what came before it.\n\n    Blocks, in order: coaching rules | athlete profile | one block per fact | today's date.\n    - Breakpoint after the profile: rules + profile are byte-identical across messages and save_fact calls.\n    - Breakpoint on the last fact: facts are append-only, so after save_fact the previous request's\n      prefix (ending at the old last fact) is still a prefix; the cache lookback finds it and only the\n      new fact is written. This also keeps the cached prefix above the model's minimum cacheable length,\n      which rules + profile alone may not reach.\n    - The date goes after the last breakpoint because it changes daily.\n    \"\"\"\n    blocks = [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n              {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_profile(a), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n    blocks += [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": f\"- {f}\"} for f in a.facts]\n    if a.facts:\n        blocks[-1][\"cache_control\"] = {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n    else:\n        blocks.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"- (none yet)\"})\n    blocks.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": f\"Today: {today.isoformat()} ({today.strftime('%A')})\"})\n    return blocks\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\nCORE_TOOLS = [\n7 requests ok; final system blocks: ['You are Pace, an endurance coa'