{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdHujccaH3AzQKf1wjjb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"After a `save_fact`, the bot no longer re-caches the whole system prompt. The next call should read the old prompt from cache and only write the new fact (a few dozen tokens). I haven't confirmed this against the real API; I only ran it against a fake client. The changes are all in `bot.py`, and ANSWER.md has the full write-up.\n\n**Why it happened:** the system prompt was one block (instructions, athlete profile and facts) with one cache marker at the end. `save_fact` added to the fact list in the middle of `reply()`, and the prompt was rebuilt on every round. So the next round sent a different block, nothing matched the cache, and all ~1000 tokens were written again.\n\n**Why I didn't just move the marker to the end of the instructions:** tools plus instructions come to about 950–1000 tokens. That's probably under Sonnet 4.5's 1024-token minimum for caching, in which case the marker is silently ignored and nothing gets cached at all.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Prompt split into blocks:** coaching rules, then the athlete profile, then one block per fact, then today's date.\n  - One cache marker sits on the profile, which never changes when a fact is saved.\n  - A second marker sits on the last fact. Facts are only ever added at the end, so the previous call's cached text is still at the start of the new prompt and the API finds it. That cached part is also over the 1024 minimum.\n  - The date now comes after both markers, so a new day doesn't break the cache either.\n- **Prompt built once per message:** rounds inside one `reply()` now send identical prompts. The model already knows the new fact from its own tool call; the next message picks it up.\n\n**Testing:** I made no API calls. A throwaway script outside the repo ran five messages, two with `save_fact`, through a fake client. It confirmed:\n- the rules and profile blocks never change;\n- each call starts with the previous call's cached text;\n- rounds within a message are identical;\n- there are at most 4 cache markers.\n\nTo confirm with real usage, look at `logs/usage.jsonl` after you deploy. The call after a `save_fact` should show `cache_read_input_tokens` close to the old total and `cache_creation_input_tokens` of only a few dozen tokens.\n\n**Worth knowing:**\n- **Tool filtering also breaks the cache.** Tools come before the system prompt, so a message that adds or drops `plan_week` or `predict_race` compared with the previous one also misses the cache. NOTES.md says to keep the filtering, so I left it. Always sending the same tool list would fix this if the cost matters.\n- **Athletes with no facts** may get no caching, because rules plus profile alone may be under 1024 tokens. That's no worse than before in practice.\n- **Secrets are committed to the repo.** `README.md` contains what looks like a real Anthropic API key, and `config/bot.toml` holds the Telegram token. I didn't touch them, but they should be revoked, replaced, and removed from git history."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1611,"cache_read_input_tokens":33698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1611},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79c4f181-d7dd-4edc-a7ae-19e07937d4fb","uuid":"695e14cd-04ea-436d-b206-064155aa0854","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:13:10.482Z","request_id":"req_011CgdHujPhxYTKawB2Ma5zm"}
